# Grain Send — 96 bpm, A minor. A demo of the granular send: two tracks
# feed one grain engine on its own bus (`gran_send=`), whose knobs sit on
# the `grains` line, and the cloud comes back into the mix ahead of the
# reverb.
#
#   beats  0-8    DRY     a plucked string and felt keys, nothing sent
#   beats  8-16   SEND    both open their sends: a thin cloud of grains
#                         on the octaves and the fifth of what they play
#   beats 16-24   THICK   the cloud thickens to 200 grains a second, half
#                         of them backwards
#   beats 24-32   HOLD    the send's buffer freezes on the last chord;
#                         the keys stop and the string drops to a low A
#                         under the held cloud

bpm 96
gate 0.95
tail 4

section DRY 0..8
section SEND 8..16
section THICK 16..24
section HOLD 24..32

automate reverb_wet
0.3

grains gran_size=70 gran_density=12 gran_pos=0.4 gran_spray=0.6 gran_pitches=0,12,7,-12 gran_pan_scatter=0.9 gran_jitter=1

track wire string vel=0.8
(A2:2 E3:2 C3:2 G2:2)x3 A1:8
automate wire.gran_send
0 >8 0.7

track keys patch=feltkeys vel=0.6
(A3:0.5 E4:0.5 C5:0.5 E4:0.5)x12 R:8
automate keys.gran_send
0 >8 0.4

automate grains.gran_density
12 >16 12 200:8@exp
automate grains.gran_reverse
0 >16 0.5
automate grains.gran_freeze
0 >24 1
